SECTION B1 -- ORBIT CLOSURE ON A SINGLE PLANE
========================================================================
same-sign pair {++}: M = [[0, 1], [-1, 0]];  exp(2*pi*M) = [[1, 0], [0, 1]];  equals identity: True
same-sign pair {--}: M = [[0, 1], [-1, 0]];  exp(2*pi*M) = [[1, 0], [0, 1]];  equals identity: True
mixed pair {+-}: M = [[0, 1], [1, 0]]
  exp(t*M) = [[cosh(t), sinh(t)], [sinh(t), cosh(t)]]
  trace(exp(t*M)) simplifies to: 2*cosh(t)
  [check] trace(exp(t*M)) == 2*cosh(t): True
  [check] exact identity 2*cosh(t) - 2 == 4*sinh(t/2)^2: True
  [check] sinh(t/2) > 0 for t > 0 (sympy assumption engine): True
  => trace(exp(t*M)) = 2*cosh(t) = 2 + 4*sinh(t/2)^2 > 2 = trace(1) for all t>0,
     hence exp(t*M) != identity for every t > 0: the K-orbit never closes.
checks performed in B1: 6, failures: 0
VERDICT: OK -- orbit closes (exp(2*pi*M) = 1 exactly) iff the pair is same-sign ({++} and {--} both verified); for a mixed pair trace(exp(t*M)) = 2*cosh(t) > 2 for all t > 0, so exp(t*M) is never the identity

